Aim

To install Docker and run basic Docker containers to understand container fundamentals.

Theory (Short)

Docker is a containerization platform used to build, run, and manage applications in isolated environments called containers.
Containers are lightweight and run applications with all dependencies, ensuring consistency across systems.
Docker commands help in creating, running, and managing containers and images.

Steps
Step 1: Check Docker Installation
docker --version

Check service:

docker info
Step 2: Run Hello World Container
docker run hello-world

Output shows Docker is working.

Step 3: Pull Ubuntu Image
docker pull ubuntu
Step 4: Run Ubuntu Container
docker run -it ubuntu

Inside container:

ls
pwd
exit
Step 5: List Docker Images
docker images
Step 6: List Running Containers
docker ps

All containers:

docker ps -a
Step 7: Remove Container
docker rm container_id
